## Summary

- Extracts a `defineEnum()` helper function to replace 17 repetitive TypeScript-style IIFE enum blocks in `agent_pb.js`
- Eliminates all 12 `qlty:similar-code` smells flagged by the daily quality sweep
- Net reduction: -195 lines in the enum section (433 → 238 lines)

## What changed

`.agents/plugins/opencode-aidevops/cursor/proto/agent_pb.js`

Before (repeated 17 times with different enum names):
```js
export var MouseButton;
(function (MouseButton) {
    MouseButton[MouseButton["UNSPECIFIED"] = 0] = "UNSPECIFIED";
    MouseButton[MouseButton["LEFT"] = 1] = "LEFT";
    // ...
})(MouseButton || (MouseButton = {}));
```

After:
```js
export var MouseButton;
defineEnum(MouseButton || (MouseButton = {}), [
    [0, "UNSPECIFIED"],
    [1, "LEFT"],
    // ...
]);
```

## Verification

- `node --check` passes (syntax valid)
- `qlty smells .agents/plugins/opencode-aidevops/cursor/proto/agent_pb.js` reports 0 findings (was 12)
- Runtime behaviour verified: bidirectional enum lookups (`EnumName["KEY"]` and `EnumName[value]`) produce identical results

## No behaviour changes

Pure structural refactor. The `defineEnum` helper replicates the exact same bidirectional assignment the IIFE pattern produces. All exported enum variables remain identical at runtime.

Closes #6555

